---
import TreatmentPage from "../../../components/TreatmentPage.astro";

const T = "/services/fertility-treatment";
const A = "/services/assessment";

const page = {
  slug: "hormonal-analysis",
  name: "Hormonal Analysis",
  title: "Fertility Hormone Test (AMH, FSH, LH) | Kamran Fertility Clinic",
  description: "Discuss fertility hormone tests such as AMH, FSH, LH, TSH and prolactin with Dr. Kamran Saleem. Plan the right tests and understand your results.",
  eyebrow: "Hormonal Analysis",
  h1: "Fertility Hormone Assessment and Test Planning",
  waText: "Hello, I would like to book a hormone assessment with Dr. Kamran Saleem.",
  ctaLabel: "Book an assessment",
  heroSub: [
    "A fertility hormone assessment reviews whether selected blood tests may help investigate reproductive concerns in women and men.",
    "The consultation focuses on choosing relevant tests, planning their timing, and understanding how results fit your overall evaluation.",
  ].join(" "),
  leadIn: [
    { rich: ["Hormone testing is one part of a wider fertility evaluation. The tests selected depend on your history, symptoms and previous results. Explore the related ", ["Fertility Assessment & Diagnosis", A], " pathway, or read the educational guide ", ["Hormone Test for Fertility", "/resources/hormone-test--for-fertility"], "."] },
  ],
  sections: [
    {
      id: "hormone-assessment-questions",
      title: "What a Fertility Hormone Assessment Reviews",
      intro: "Hormone tests are selected to answer a clinical question, not as a routine full panel.",
      icon: "flask",
      body: [
        "Hormones influence ovulation, menstrual cycles and sperm production. A clinician reviews your history and decides whether blood tests could help explain a concern or guide the next step.",
        { ul: [
          "Irregular or absent periods or possible ovulation concerns",
          "Questions about ovarian reserve, particularly with increasing age or before treatment decisions",
          "Symptoms that may point to thyroid or prolactin problems",
          "Male reproductive concerns where hormone testing may be relevant",
        ] },
      ],
    },
    {
      id: "which-tests-may-be-discussed",
      title: "Which Hormones May Be Considered?",
      intro: "The tests depend on the symptoms, cycle pattern and prior findings.",
      icon: "clipboard",
      body: [
        { ul: [
          "AMH (anti-Müllerian hormone) as one indicator of ovarian reserve, which relates to the number of remaining eggs rather than egg quality",
          "FSH, LH and estradiol, often interpreted together in selected ovarian assessments",
          "Progesterone when checking a specific ovulation question",
          "TSH (thyroid) or prolactin when history suggests they may be relevant",
          "Testosterone, FSH or LH for selected male reproductive concerns",
        ] },
        "No single hormone test can predict whether a pregnancy will happen. Each result answers a narrow question and has to be read with your age, history and other findings.",
      ],
    },
    {
      id: "hormones-in-women",
      title: "Hormone Testing for Women",
      intro: "In women, hormone tests mainly help investigate ovulation, cycle irregularity and ovarian reserve.",
      icon: "calendar",
      body: [
        "Some female hormone tests are done at a particular point in the menstrual cycle, often early in the cycle for FSH, LH and estradiol, while AMH can usually be measured at any time. Progesterone timing depends on when ovulation is expected.",
        { rich: ["Cycle-timing questions are covered further on our ", ["ovulation test", `${A}/ovulation-test`], " page, and a broader review is available through ", ["female fertility assessment", `${A}/female-fertility-test`], "."] },
      ],
    },
    {
      id: "hormones-in-men",
      title: "Hormone Testing for Men",
      intro: "Hormone tests are not needed for every man, but they can help when sperm results or symptoms point that way.",
      icon: "compare",
      body: [
        "Sperm production depends on signals from the brain and the testes. Testosterone, FSH and LH may be considered when a semen analysis is abnormal, when sperm counts are very low, or when there are symptoms such as low libido or erectile concerns.",
        { rich: ["Semen testing is usually the first step; see ", ["semen analysis", `${A}/semen-analysis`], " and ", ["male fertility testing", `${A}/male-fertility-test`], ", or the broader ", ["male infertility assessment", `${A}/male-infertility`], "."] },
      ],
    },
    {
      id: "timing-and-preparation",
      title: "Timing and Preparation",
      intro: "Some tests depend on cycle timing or the time of day.",
      icon: "calendar",
      body: [
        "Before testing, confirm the requested date and preparation with the clinician or laboratory. Share your cycle dates, medicines, supplements, recent hormonal contraception and previous results so timing can be planned appropriately.",
        { rich: ["For the educational overview of hormone tests, see ", ["Hormone Test for Fertility", "/resources/hormone-test--for-fertility"], "."] },
      ],
    },
    {
      id: "reviewing-hormone-results",
      title: "Reviewing Hormone Results",
      intro: "A laboratory range is only one part of interpretation.",
      icon: "compare",
      body: [
        "Results are considered with your symptoms, age, cycle timing, medical history and any other investigations such as ultrasound or semen analysis. An isolated value may need context or repeat testing before a conclusion is drawn.",
        { rich: ["Hormone findings can lead to further evaluation or to a discussion of ", ["fertility treatment", T], " options where appropriate. Related pages include ", ["ovulation assessment", `${A}/ovulation-test`], ", ", ["female fertility assessment", `${A}/female-fertility-test`], " and ", ["male infertility assessment", `${A}/male-infertility`], ". You may also find ", ["PCOS and Fertility", "/resources/pcos-and-fertility"], " helpful."] },
      ],
    },
  ],
  faqs: [
    { q: "Do I need a complete fertility hormone panel?", a: "Not necessarily. The clinician selects tests based on your history and the question being investigated." },
    { q: "Can hormone tests be done on any day?", a: "Some can, while others depend on menstrual-cycle timing or time of day. Confirm timing for the specific tests ordered." },
    { q: "Can a hormone result alone diagnose infertility?", a: "No. Results are interpreted alongside your history and other relevant findings." },
    { q: "What does an AMH test tell me?", a: "AMH is commonly used as an indicator of ovarian reserve. It does not measure egg quality and does not on its own predict whether you can conceive naturally." },
    { q: "Do men need hormone tests for fertility?", a: "Only in some cases, for example when semen results are abnormal or symptoms suggest a hormonal cause. A clinician can advise whether testing is useful." },
    { q: "Should I stop my medicines before a hormone test?", a: "Do not stop any prescribed medicine without medical advice. Tell the clinician and the laboratory what you take so results can be read correctly." },
  ],
  closingHeading: "Fertility Hormone Assessment with Dr. Kamran Saleem",
  closingParas: [
    "Dr. Kamran Saleem can review your history and available reports, discuss whether hormone testing is appropriate, and explain possible next steps. The exact tests and plan depend on your individual circumstances.",
    "You can ask about the consultation and any separate test fees before confirming an appointment.",
  ],
  resources: [
    { href: "/resources/hormone-test--for-fertility", category: "Fertility Assessment", title: "Hormone Test for Fertility" },
    { href: "/resources/pcos-and-fertility", category: "Fertility Assessment", title: "PCOS and Fertility" },
    { href: "/resources/ovulation-test", category: "Fertility Assessment", title: "Ovulation Test: How to Track Your Cycle" },
  ],
  close: {
    heading: "Need Help Choosing the Right Assessment?",
    body: "Share your symptoms, cycle history or previous reports when booking so the consultation can focus on your questions.",
    cta: "Book an assessment",
  },
};
---

<TreatmentPage {...page} />
